{
  "note": "Flyby path (Latch). Stops are anchored on the export, never on scene objects; Flyby resolves each to a camera key (look target, yaw, pitch, distance, fov) and eases between them, lifting the eye on long moves so it does not drive through buildings. kind: fit (yaw/pitch/fov framing `frame` with `margin` (default 1.05; below 1 crops): '*', a layer, an element id or an id prefix ending in '*'), play (the export's play camera: orthographic `zoom` at its pitch and yaw on its focus; approached by a dolly zoom), street (eye at eyeHeight on the busiest street-level shopfront run of `street`, `out` m in front of the shops, looking along them), deck (the largest deck of `level`, eye at eyeHeight looking along its long axis), station (eye on the platform of station `id` looking along it and past its end), along (eye on element `id`'s long axis at fraction `at`, `side` m to its right, eyeHeight above its top, looking `ahead` m along it; `reverse` 1 turns it round), megas (one fit per megastructure, yaw + i * yawStep, or `yaws` per id). hold = seconds stopped (the camera drifts `drift` deg/s), travel = seconds to the next stop. shadowDistance (m) is applied to the URP asset while the flyby runs (restored after). render: frames for out/shots/flyby/. Brief 007 E adds: rail (ride sky rail `id` from `from` to `to` metres along its line at `speed` m/s, eye `eyeHeight` over the beam top, keys every `step` m at constant speed; contact images at its two ends) and toward (eye `eyeHeight` over element `from`'s top, looking at element `to`, or at height `lookZ` over it). render.ffmpeg: the encoder Render Flyby Frames pipes every frame into for flyby.mp4. Brief 007 round 2: spacehq-crown (the atom crown over the fluted tower), liner-dock frames the OceanLiner beside its terminal, bay-horizon looks out over the quay to the bay sector and the land arms. render.crf / render.preset: H.264 rate control (CRF 25, slow: about 200 MB for 3.5 min of 1080p30; CRF 18 made 397 MB).",
